<tr id="S6.T3.2.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S6.T3.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:2pt;padding-bottom:2pt;">
<span id="S6.T3.2.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:119.5pt;">
<span id="S6.T3.2.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.T3.2.1.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Runtime Semantics as a Signal</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S6.T3.2.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:2pt;padding-bottom:2pt;">
<span id="S6.T3.2.1.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:204.9pt;">
<span id="S6.T3.2.1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">QuickSilver uses L2 drift and entropy to measure token convergence and salience, aligning efficiency with linguistic intuitions and information-theoretic properties.</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S6.T3.2.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:2pt;padding-bottom:2pt;">
<span id="S6.T3.2.1.2.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:156.5pt;">
<span id="S6.T3.2.1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">Bridges representation dynamics with compute allocation, paving the way for semantic-saliency-aware inference.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T3.2.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S6.T3.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_l ltx_border_r" style="padding-top:2pt;padding-bottom:2pt;">
<span id="S6.T3.2.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:119.5pt;">
